      "rationale": "Both reviews agree on the reading: phase, with the bright primary-cementite needles as the flakes. The current best already uses flake_phase=bright, so the reading and phase stay as they are. The twin is untrusted (minority fraction ratio 0.58, contrast ratio 0.42, flake recall 0, precision 0.03), so its scores support nothing and these start params will be judged only by the next review of the real drawing. I therefore change only three params, each tied to something the reviewer saw. (1) Specks of matrix lamellae dominate n=359 and pull the median aspect ratio down to 2.1. min_area_px goes to 500, the maximum allowed; this is a 2.5x increase rather than the 5-10x the reviewer suggested, because 500 is the cap. min_aspect_for_orientation stays at 3.0; the reviewer suggested 4, but the parameter's maximum is 3. (2) A slightly higher phase_offset, 0.10, thins the bright mask so that plates detach from the bright eutectic network. The reviewer suggested a morphological opening, which this method does not offer; this is the closest available control. (3) Needle pieces get different colours at crossings, a sign that pieces of crossing needles are merged off-axis. merge_max_offaxis_deg=15 restricts merges to pieces lying end to end, close to the reviewer's request to re-join only collinear fragments. Not changed, and stated plainly: no parameter splits X-shaped crossings by orientation. The skeleton branch test will still grey out merged crossings, and the watershed will still cut needles at crossings, so coverage will likely stay low (perhaps 0.2-0.35). The aspect-ratio and length numbers for the needles will very probably remain unusable. If the next review still shows crossings cut or greyed, the honest conclusion is that this method cannot measure needle aspect ratio on this set; at most a structure-tensor S, or tensor_order_parameter on the bright mask, could be reported. The closest earlier set, needles_L23 (distance 0), failed (rotation check 0